VenusOS-WiFiAP
==============

Cerbo GX-style WiFi Access Point for Venus OS on Raspberry Pi, with 4G/NAT
internet sharing. The WiFi stays a client (wlan0) AND becomes an access
point (ap0) at the same time - concurrent STA+AP, like on a Cerbo GX.

No hostapd needed: the AP runs on the image's wpa_supplicant (built with
CONFIG_AP). The package installs the native "hostapd" service template, so
venus-platform publishes the real Victron toggle: the AP is switched on/off
from the stock UI (both GUI v1 and gui-v2), and the AP password can be
managed through /Settings/Services/AccessPointPassword like on a Cerbo.

Validated on Raspberry Pi 5 (BCM43455) / Venus OS 3.75. Works on the
Pi 3 (BCM43438) as well.

## Requirements

- Venus OS v3.50 or later
- Raspberry Pi with the built-in Broadcom WiFi (Pi 3/4/5)
- SetupHelper (kwindrem) installed

## Installation

Via SetupHelper PackageManager (recommended):
  GitHub: florent1080/VenusOS-WiFiAP

Manual:
  cd /data/VenusOS-WiFiAP && bash setup install auto

After install the AP is ENABLED by default (Victron behaviour: the setting
/Settings/Services/AccessPoint is created with default 1).

## Configuration

Toggle in the UI: Settings > Wi-Fi > "Create access point".

Edit /data/wifi-ap/wifi-ap.conf for the rest:

  SSID=ZeVan              # WiFi network name
  PASSWORD=victron1234    # fallback WPA2 password (8-63 chars) - only used
                          # when /Settings/Services/AccessPointPassword is empty
  CHANNEL=1               # fallback channel (1-13), used when wlan0 is not
                          # connected; otherwise the AP follows wlan0's channel
  AP_IP=192.168.0.1       # Pi gateway IP on the AP network

After editing: svc -t /service/hostapd  (or flip the UI toggle off/on)

## Connecting

- Connect your device to WiFi "ZeVan" (or your custom SSID)
- Your device gets IP 192.168.0.x via DHCP
- Internet is shared with NAT toward whatever uplink is active (4G wwan0
  in the van, or the wlan0/eth0 connection elsewhere), with TCP MSS
  clamping for cellular MTUs
- SSH to the Pi: ssh root@192.168.0.1

## How it works

  UI toggle -> com.victronenergy.platform /Services/AccessPoint/Enabled
    -> /Settings/Services/AccessPoint (localsettings)
    -> venus-platform -> svectl -s hostapd -> /service/hostapd
    -> template run -> /data/VenusOS-WiFiAP/files/wifi-ap-run
    -> ap0 + wpa_supplicant (mode AP) + dnsmasq (DHCP) + iptables (NAT)

venus-platform only publishes the toggle when
/opt/victronenergy/service-templates/conf/hostapd.conf exists - that marker
and the template are what this package installs. A password change on
/Settings/Services/AccessPointPassword restarts the service automatically
(native venus-platform behaviour).

## Notes

- Single radio: when wlan0 is connected, the AP runs on the same channel
  (or cross-band, the firmware time-slices).
- Known firmware issue raspberrypi/linux#7092 (BCM43455, kernel 6.12): the
  firmware can wedge during AP restarts with clients around - a password
  change restarts the AP (native venus-platform behaviour) and can trigger
  it. The bundled wifi-watchdog service detects the wedge and self-heals
  (driver reload, then a recovery reboot at worst); forensic snapshots go
  to /data/log/wifi-ap/wedge.log.
- wifi-ap.conf is preserved on reinstall / Venus OS update
- Logs: tail -F /var/log/hostapd/current
- connman ignores ap0 (NetworkInterfaceBlacklist includes "ap")
